    {
      "id": "claim_b75097d7e3a349fea34123da9af7d6b0",
      "statement": "End-to-end IPTV connectivity requires three cooperating artifacts: (1) an OPNsense LAN pass rule for the RTSP control channel on TCP/UDP port 554 from LAN network to WAN address, (2) a second pass rule admitting inbound UDP from the FRITZ!Box IP with source ports 5000-5010 to the LAN net on the FRITZ!Box-facing interface (without which OPNsense's default-deny drops the unsolicited RTP), and (3) a 1:1 NAT mapping external subnet 192.168.180.0 to internal network 192.168.178.0, paired with a static IPv4 route in the FRITZ!Box sending traffic for 192.168.180.0 to the firewall's WAN IP as gateway.",
      "evidence": [
